{
  "$schema": "../../schema/app.schema.json",
  "id": "pika-studio-director",
  "name": "Pika Studio Director",
  "section": "video",
  "pack": "video-h3",
  "status": "ready",
  "summary": "Pika Flex locked: lcm + 6-step sigmas, Material Planner segments, auto/ref2va/fl2va adapter, Production profiles and optional RelayVSR.",
  "higgsfield_feature": "AI Director",
  "source": {
    "template": "RiverField_Director_studio.json (Pika-locked variant)",
    "comfyui": "0.43.0",
    "notes": "Same graph as studio-director, with the recipe the Pika Flex LoRA is distilled for: sampler lcm, ManualSigmas 1.0,0.972973,0.923077,0.8,0.571429,0.333333,0.0, the Pika Flex adapter at 1.0, minimax_h3 int8 + p-H3 image int8 encoder + lynnreal light VAE, SLA on Sol-Attn. The only model choice is the adapter: ref2va (minimax_h3_ref2va + pika_h3_flex_ref2va) for reference material, fl2va (minimax_h3_fl2va + pika_h3_flex_fl2va) for plain text-to-video — each LoRA moves with the H3 model it was distilled for, on the same lcm + 6-step schedule. Sampler and sigma choices are not exposed: this app cannot be broken by a wrong preset. Use studio-director when you want to experiment with other models or schedules. SelfLift two-stage requires the Euler sampler; the Pika LoRA is lcm-distilled and collapses with euler (measured), so two-stage is not offered here. Use studio-director with a non-LCM model for two-stage."
  },
